Implement user story AMSD-1820: [Mozio] - Promo code discount amount not displayed for return trip segment in email confirmation

## Story Description
The promo code discount amount is not displayed as expected for return trip tickets in the Mozio email confirmation. When a return trip order has a promo code applied, the discount amount fails to render for the return trip segment. This fix ensures the promo code discount data is correctly passed from the order payload to the email template context for all trip segments and rendered consistently in the email output.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Given a return trip ticket order with a promo code applied to both legs, when the Mozio email confirmation is generated, then the promo code discount amount MUST be displayed for both the outbound and return trip segments.
- Given a one-way trip ticket order with a promo code applied, when the Mozio email confirmation is generated, then the promo code discount amount MUST be displayed for the single trip segment (regression check).
- Given a return trip ticket order with no promo code applied, when the Mozio email confirmation is generated, then no promo discount line item should appear for either trip segment.
- Given a return trip ticket order with a promo code that applies only to the outbound leg, when the Mozio email confirmation is generated, then the promo discount should appear only on the outbound segment and not on the return segment.
- Given a return trip ticket order with a promo code that applies only to the return leg, when the Mozio email confirmation is generated, then the promo discount should appear only on the return segment and not on the outbound segment.
- Given a return trip ticket order with a promo code applied to both legs, when the Mozio email confirmation is generated, then the discount amount displayed for each segment must match the corresponding discount value in the order payload.
- Given a return trip ticket order with a promo code applied, when the email confirmation HTML is rendered, then the promo discount line item format (label, currency symbol, amount) must be consistent between outbound and return segments.
- Given a return trip ticket order with a promo code that results in a zero-value discount on one or both legs, when the Mozio email confirmation is generated, then the promo discount line item must still be displayed for the applicable segment(s) showing the zero-value amount rather than being omitted.
- Given a return trip ticket order with a promo code applied where the outbound and return legs use different currencies, when the Mozio email confirmation is generated, then each segment's promo discount must display the amount in that segment's own currency with the correct currency symbol.





